 "number": 131,
 "title": "Palindrome Partitioning",
 "slug": "palindrome-partitioning",
 "category": "backtracking",
 "difficulty": "Medium",
 "url": "https://leetcode.com/problems/palindrome-partitioning/",
 "pattern": "Backtracking over cut positions",
 "statement": "Given a string `s`, cut it into pieces so that **every piece is a palindrome** (reads the same forwards and backwards). Return all possible ways to do this.",
 "example": {
  "input": "s = \"aab\"",
  "output": "[[\"a\",\"a\",\"b\"],[\"aa\",\"b\"]]",
  "why": "a | a | b and aa | b. The pieces 'ab' and 'aab' are not palindromes, so no other cut works."
 },
 "more": [
  {
   "input": "s = \"a\"",
   "output": "[[\"a\"]]"
  },
  {
   "input": "s = \"aba\"",
   "output": "[[\"a\",\"b\",\"a\"],[\"aba\"]]"
  },
  {
   "input": "s = \"abc\"",
   "output": "[[\"a\",\"b\",\"c\"]]"
  }
 ],
 "idea": [
  "Decide the pieces from left to right. The first piece is some prefix `s[start:end]` — try every possible end.",
  "A prefix that is **not** a palindrome can never be part of an answer, so that branch is dropped immediately.",
  "If it is a palindrome, take it as a piece and solve the same problem for the rest of the string. Reaching the end of `s` means every piece was fine → save the partition. Then undo and try a longer piece."
 ],
 "code": "class Solution:\n    def partition(self, s: str) -> List[List[str]]:\n        def is_palindrome(sub):\n            return sub == sub[::-1]\n\n        def backtrack(start, partition):\n            if start == len(s):\n                result.append(partition[:])  # Append a copy of the current partition\n                return\n\n            for end in range(start + 1, len(s) + 1):\n                sub = s[start:end]\n                if is_palindrome(sub):\n                    partition.append(sub)\n                    backtrack(end, partition)\n                    partition.pop()  # Backtrack\n\n        result = []\n        backtrack(0, [])\n        return result",
 "complexity": {
  "time": "O(n · 2ⁿ)",
  "timeWhy": "There are 2ⁿ⁻¹ ways to place cuts; checking and copying pieces costs O(n) each.",
  "space": "O(n)",
  "spaceWhy": "Recursion depth and the current partition are at most n (not counting the output)."
 },
